title: Proposition 23
---
order: 23
---
short_label: VII.23
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two numbers are relatively prime, then any number which measures one of them is relatively prime to the remaining number.
----
proof:

Let *A* and *B* be two numbers relatively prime, and let any number *C* measure *A.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="150" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.23 diagram" src="propVII23.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
